      'Darkforme-Glacier-Maw': 'The Glacier-Maw sells the Frost-March as a place where the landscape itself becomes an ambush predator beneath the ice.',
      'Darkforme-Skirmisher': 'Skirmishers fit Hinterland as a roaming pressure unit: fast, opportunistic, and exactly the sort of threat that makes interior roads feel contested.',
      'Darkforme-Harrier': 'Harriers sell the region as watched territory, giving the atlas a believable aerial scout presence over open routes and border seams.',
      'Darkforme-Slinger': 'The slinger works here as a mobile ambush threat, reinforcing that Hinterland is curated around travel risk rather than a single landmark monster.',
